ted matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1017 #edb/ref 17592186314954 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1089 "q-10633" 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+z=2 \\\\  & 2y+z=0 \\\\  & -x+2y+z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1113 #uuid "981ba9f9-5df7-5209-b75f-a32164a752ed" 13194139534853 true] [17592186314953 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}